---
slug: admin/support
layout: modules/support/agent
metadata:
  title: Support
---
{%- comment -%}
  The ticket list. A controller: it gathers everything and hands finished
  arrays to the partials, which render and do not query.

  Counting happens here, in Liquid, over one array of open tickets. The
  sidebar alone wants a count per view, per status and per department, and
  the tabs want one per priority. Asking the database for each would be
  seventeen queries on every page load.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # platformos-check-disable DeprecatedTag
  include 'modules/support/helpers/require_permission', do: 'support.access', entity: null
  # platformos-check-enable DeprecatedTag

  function tokens = 'modules/support/helpers/ui/tokens'
  function current_profile = 'modules/user/helpers/current_profile'
  function agent = 'modules/support/helpers/current_agent'
  function can_rerank = 'modules/support/helpers/can', do: 'support.tickets.rerank', entity: null
  function can_manage_settings = 'modules/support/helpers/can', do: 'support.settings.manage', entity: null
  function settings = 'modules/support/queries/settings/get'
  function statuses = 'modules/support/queries/statuses/search', kind: null
  function all_agents = 'modules/support/queries/agents/all'

  graphql department_result = 'modules/support/departments/search', limit: 50, page: 1, id: null, slug: null, inbound_address: null
  assign departments = department_result.records.results

  comment
    A host superadmin with no agent record still gets in, by the same
    break glass rule the guard uses, and sees every department.
  endcomment
  assign viewer = agent
  if agent == blank
    assign viewer = { "role": "admin", "department_ids": [] }
  endif

  function queue = 'modules/support/queries/tickets/queue', agent: viewer, statuses: statuses, limit: 500

  assign contact_ids = []
  for ticket in queue
    assign contact_ids = contact_ids | array_add: ticket.contact_id
  endfor
  function contacts = 'modules/support/queries/contacts/by_ids', ids: contact_ids

  assign status_by_id = {}
  comment
    The sidebar lists only the statuses a ticket in this queue can be in.
    The queue holds nothing closed, so a closed status there could never
    read anything but zero, and clicking it would land on "Nothing in
    this view", which reads like a broken filter rather than an empty
    one. The board is where closed tickets are reached, behind Show
    Closed.
  endcomment
  assign sidebar_statuses = []
  for status in statuses
    assign token = tokens.statuses[status.key] | default: tokens.status_fallback
    assign status.token = token
    assign status_by_id[status.id] = status
    unless status.kind == 'closed'
      assign sidebar_statuses = sidebar_statuses | array_add: status
    endunless
  endfor

  assign department_by_id = {}
  assign department_position = 0
  for department in departments
    assign palette_index = department_position | modulo: 6
    assign department.palette = tokens.department_palette[palette_index]
    assign department.letter = department.name | slice: 0, 1 | upcase
    assign department_by_id[department.id] = department
    assign department_position = department_position | plus: 1
  endfor

  assign agent_by_user = {}
  assign agent_position = 0
  for one_agent in all_agents
    assign palette_index = agent_position | modulo: 6
    assign one_agent.palette = tokens.agent_palette[palette_index]
    assign agent_by_user[one_agent.user_id] = one_agent
    assign agent_position = agent_position | plus: 1
  endfor

  assign rows = []
  for ticket in queue
    assign ticket.contact = contacts[ticket.contact_id]
    assign ticket.status = status_by_id[ticket.status_id]
    assign ticket.department = department_by_id[ticket.department_id]
    assign ticket.assignee = agent_by_user[ticket.assignee_id]
    assign ticket.priority_token = tokens.priorities[ticket.priority]
    assign rows = rows | array_add: ticket
  endfor

  assign view = context.params.view | default: 'all'
  assign status_filter = context.params.status
  assign department_filter = context.params.department
  assign priority_filter = context.params.priority | default: 'all'
  assign group_by = context.params.group | default: 'priority'
  assign assignee_filter = context.params.assignee
  comment
    The box says "ticket #, subject or email", so an agent types #18022.
    The haystack holds the bare number, so the hash comes off here rather
    than quietly matching nothing.
  endcomment
  assign search_query = context.params.q | default: '' | strip | downcase | remove_first: '#'
  assign expanded = context.params.expand | default: '' | split: ','
  assign collapsed_groups = context.params.collapsed | default: '' | split: ','

  assign current_user_id = current_profile.user.id

  comment
    Which tickets have the search text somewhere in their conversation.
    One query before the loop rather than one per row, and empty unless
    something was typed.
  endcomment
  function body_matches = 'modules/support/queries/messages/search_bodies', query: search_query, limit: null

  comment
    One pass, four verdicts per row. Each count then uses the verdicts it
    cares about and ignores the rest, which is how a status count can
    respect the department filter without counting itself.
  endcomment
  assign counted = []
  for row in rows
    function passes_view = 'modules/support/helpers/ui/in_view', view: view, row: row, current_user_id: current_user_id

    assign passes_department = true
    if department_filter != blank and row.department.slug != department_filter
      assign passes_department = false
    endif

    assign passes_status = true
    if status_filter != blank and row.status.key != status_filter
      assign passes_status = false
    endif

    assign passes_priority = true
    if priority_filter != 'all' and row.priority_token.key != priority_filter
      assign passes_priority = false
    endif

    assign passes_assignee = true
    if assignee_filter != blank and row.assignee_id != assignee_filter
      assign passes_assignee = false
    endif

    assign passes_search = true
    if search_query != blank
      assign haystack = row.c__search | default: '' | downcase
      unless haystack contains search_query
        unless body_matches[row.id]
          assign passes_search = false
        endunless
      endunless
    endif

    assign row.passes_view = passes_view
    assign row.passes_department = passes_department
    assign row.passes_status = passes_status
    assign row.passes_priority = passes_priority
    assign row.passes_assignee = passes_assignee
    assign row.passes_search = passes_search
    assign counted = counted | array_add: row
  endfor

  assign count_mine = 0
  assign count_unassigned = 0
  assign count_needs_reply = 0
  assign count_waiting = 0
  assign count_on_hold = 0
  assign count_solved = 0
  assign count_all = counted.size
  assign status_counts = {}
  assign department_counts = {}
  assign priority_counts = {}
  assign visible = []

  for row in counted
    if row.assignee_id == current_user_id and current_user_id != blank
      assign count_mine = count_mine | plus: 1
    endif
    if row.assignee_id == blank
      assign count_unassigned = count_unassigned | plus: 1
    endif
    comment
      The view counts ignore every filter, the same way My tickets and
      Unassigned always have: a view's count is how much work is in it,
      not how much of it survives whatever is on screen right now.
    endcomment
    if row.needs_reply
      assign count_needs_reply = count_needs_reply | plus: 1
    endif
    if row.status.kind == 'pending'
      assign count_waiting = count_waiting | plus: 1
    endif
    if row.status.kind == 'on_hold'
      assign count_on_hold = count_on_hold | plus: 1
    endif
    if row.status.kind == 'solved'
      assign count_solved = count_solved | plus: 1
    endif

    assign department_key = row.department.slug
    assign previous = department_counts[department_key] | default: 0
    assign department_counts[department_key] = previous | plus: 1

    if row.passes_view and row.passes_department and row.passes_priority and row.passes_assignee and row.passes_search
      assign status_key = row.status.key
      assign previous = status_counts[status_key] | default: 0
      assign status_counts[status_key] = previous | plus: 1
    endif

    if row.passes_view and row.passes_department and row.passes_status and row.passes_assignee and row.passes_search
      assign priority_key = row.priority_token.key
      assign previous = priority_counts[priority_key] | default: 0
      assign priority_counts[priority_key] = previous | plus: 1

      if row.passes_priority
        assign visible = visible | array_add: row
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    What the All priorities tab counts. The per priority tabs each count
    what the other filters allow, so this has to agree with them: showing
    the whole queue's total beside them reads as a bug.
  endcomment
  assign priority_total = 0
  for priority_token in tokens.priorities
    assign one_count = priority_counts[priority_token.key] | default: 0
    assign priority_total = priority_total | plus: one_count
  endfor

  comment
    Top three per group, but only in the view that shows everything at
    once. Ask for one priority or one status and you asked to see them
    all, so the cap lifts.
  endcomment
  assign limit_groups = false
  if priority_filter == 'all' and status_filter == blank
    assign limit_groups = true
  endif

  assign groups = []

  if group_by == 'status'
    for status in statuses
      assign group_rows = []
      for row in visible
        if row.status_id == status.id
          assign group_rows = group_rows | array_add: row
        endif
      endfor

      if group_rows.size > 0
        assign group = { "key": status.key, "label": status.name, "kind": "status", "status": status, "rows": group_rows, "total": group_rows.size }
        assign groups = groups | array_add: group
      endif
    endfor
  else
    for priority_token in tokens.priorities
      if priority_filter != 'all' and priority_token.key != priority_filter
        continue
      endif

      assign group_rows = []
      for row in visible
        if row.priority_token.key == priority_token.key
          assign group_rows = group_rows | array_add: row
        endif
      endfor

      if group_rows.size > 0
        assign group = { "key": priority_token.key, "label": priority_token.label, "kind": "priority", "priority": priority_token, "rows": group_rows, "total": group_rows.size }
        assign groups = groups | array_add: group
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign prepared_groups = []
  for group in groups
    assign is_collapsed = false
    if collapsed_groups contains group.key
      assign is_collapsed = true
    endif

    assign is_expanded = false
    if expanded contains group.key
      assign is_expanded = true
    endif

    assign has_more = false
    if limit_groups and group.total > 3
      assign has_more = true
    endif

    assign shown_rows = group.rows
    if is_collapsed
      assign shown_rows = []
    elsif has_more and is_expanded == false
      assign shown_rows = group.rows | slice: 0, 3
    endif

    assign group.is_collapsed = is_collapsed
    assign group.is_expanded = is_expanded
    assign group.has_more = has_more
    assign group.shown_rows = shown_rows
    assign prepared_groups = prepared_groups | array_add: group
  endfor

  assign shown_total = 0
  for group in prepared_groups
    assign shown_total = shown_total | plus: group.total
  endfor

  function view_label = 'modules/support/helpers/ui/view_label', view: view

  assign heading = view_label
  if status_filter != blank
    assign filtered_status = null
    for status in statuses
      if status.key == status_filter
        assign filtered_status = status
      endif
    endfor
    assign heading = filtered_status.name
  elsif department_filter != blank
    for department in departments
      if department.slug == department_filter
        assign heading = department.name
      endif
    endfor
  endif
  if priority_filter != 'all'
    assign heading = heading | append: ' · ' | append: priority_filter
  endif

  comment
    Counted in the translation rather than here, so a language that needs
    more than two forms, or puts the number elsewhere in the sentence, can
    have them without this page changing.
  endcomment
  assign subtitle = 'modules/support/list.count' | t: count: shown_total

  assign brand = settings.brand_name | default: 'Support'

  comment
    An agent with no departments sees an empty queue for a reason that
    has nothing to do with being on top of the work, and "All caught up"
    is the wrong congratulations.
  endcomment
  assign no_departments = false
  if agent != blank and agent.role != 'admin' and agent.department_ids == blank
    assign no_departments = true
  endif

  comment
    Where the POST endpoints send the agent back to. A path, not a full
    URL: helpers/redirect_back refuses anything that is not a path on this
    site, so that a crafted form field cannot become an open redirect.
  endcomment
  function return_to = 'modules/support/helpers/ui/queue_url', overrides: {}
-%}
{% render 'modules/support/list/sidebar',
  brand: brand,
  tokens: tokens,
  statuses: sidebar_statuses,
  departments: departments,
  status_counts: status_counts,
  department_counts: department_counts,
  count_mine: count_mine,
  count_unassigned: count_unassigned,
  count_needs_reply: count_needs_reply,
  count_waiting: count_waiting,
  count_on_hold: count_on_hold,
  count_solved: count_solved,
  count_all: count_all,
  view: view,
  status_filter: status_filter,
  department_filter: department_filter,
  can_manage_settings: can_manage_settings,
  current_profile: current_profile,
  show_statuses: true
%}
<main class="pos-support-main">
  {% render 'modules/support/list/header',
    heading: heading,
    subtitle: subtitle,
    tokens: tokens,
    search_query: context.params.q,
    base: '/admin/support',
    screen: 'list'
  %}
  {% render 'modules/support/list/toolbar',
    tokens: tokens,
    priority_counts: priority_counts,
    priority_filter: priority_filter,
    group_by: group_by,
    all_agents: all_agents,
    assignee_filter: assignee_filter,
    priority_total: priority_total,
    can_rerank: can_rerank
  %}
  {% render 'modules/support/list/bulk', all_agents: all_agents, statuses: statuses, tokens: tokens, return_to: return_to %}
  {% render 'modules/support/list/table',
    groups: prepared_groups,
    group_by: group_by,
    tokens: tokens,
    can_rerank: can_rerank,
    shown_total: shown_total,
    count_all: count_all,
    no_departments: no_departments,
    return_to: return_to
  %}
</main>
